<title>PAKISTAN: CRICKET-PAKISTAN V ZIMBABWE SECOND TEST SCOREBOARD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-PAKISTAN V ZIMBABWE SECOND TEST SCOREBOARD.</headline>
<dateline>FAISALABAD, Pakistan 1996-10-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scoreboard on the</p>
<p>third day of the second and final test between Pakistan and</p>
<p>Zimbabwe on Saturday:</p>
<p>Zimbabwe first innings 133 (A.Flower 61; Wasim Akram 6-48)</p>
<p>Pakistan first innings 267 (Saeed Anwar 81, Moin Khan 58)</p>
<p>Zimbabwe second innings (overnight 136-3)</p>
<p> G.Flower lbw b Wasim Akram		   0</p>
<p> M.Dekker lbw b Waqar Younis		  0</p>
<p> C.Wishart c Salim Malik b Waqar Younis   7</p>
<p> D.Houghton lbw b Wasim Akram		74</p>
<p> A.Campbell c Moin Khan b Shahid Nazir   51</p>
<p> A.Flower c Saeed Anwar b Waqar Younis   23</p>
<p> G.Whittal lbw b Shahid Nazir		 0</p>
<p> P.Strang b Waqar Younis			9</p>
<p> B.Strang not out				13</p>
<p> M.Mbangwn b Wasim Akram			7</p>
<p> E.Matambanadzo lbw b Wasim Akram	   2</p>
<p> Extras (lb-9 nb-5)			    14</p>
<p> Total					    200</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-0 2-0 3-23 4-136 5-136 6-140 7-169 8-174</p>
<p>9-198</p>
<p>Bowling: Wasim Akram 18.4-4-57-4 (nb4), Waqar Younis</p>
<p>15-3-54-4 (nb1), Saqlain Mushtaq 7-1-33-0, Shahid Nazir</p>
<p>11-5-25-2, Muhammad Hussain 4-1-14-0, Salim Malik 2-0-8-0</p>
<p>Pakistan second innings</p>
<p> Saeed Anwar not out			  50</p>
<p> Aamir Sohail not out			 18</p>
<p> Extras (w-1)				    1</p>
<p> Total (for no wicket)			69</p>
<p>Bowling: Matambanadzo 5-0-27-0, Mbangwn 7-3-14-0, B.Strang</p>
<p>4.5-1-20-0 (w1), P.Strang 2-0-8-0</p>
<p>Result: Pakistan won by 10 wickets</p>
<p>Man-of-the-match: Wasim Akram</p>
<p>First test: Sheikhupura - match drawn</p>
